From: hawkff <109485367+hawkff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 05:24:54 +0000
Subject: Show plain HTTP pages as dangerous

Pages loaded over plain HTTP that were shown with the WARNING security
level now get the DANGEROUS level. Potentially trustworthy origins such as
localhost keep their level. On Android the address bar shows the "Not
secure" icon and label in red instead of the toolbar color, the toolbar
stays on screen while the page scrolls, and the page theme color is not
applied to the browser UI. Anyone on the network path can read and change
an HTTP page, and the stronger signal makes that harder to overlook, in
particular after the user continues past the HTTPS-Only Mode warning.
GrapheneOS Vanadium uses the same default.

License: GPL-2.0-or-later - https://spdx.org/licenses/GPL-2.0-or-later.html
---
 components/security_state/core/security_state.cc | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/security_state/core/security_state.cc b/components/security_state/core/security_state.cc
--- a/components/security_state/core/security_state.cc
+++ b/components/security_state/core/security_state.cc
@@ -132,7 +132,7 @@ SecurityLevel GetSecurityLevel(
         return NONE;
       }
 #endif  // !BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
-      return WARNING;
+      return DANGEROUS;
     }
     return NONE;
   }
